From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:37:49 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS] cc: Don't cache record shaders that use SharedImages

SkImages opened through the SharedImageProvider borrow their textures
only for the current raster pass. A record shader whose record opened
one was still stored in the service-side transfer cache, and a later
pass could reuse it, after the SharedImage may have been destroyed.

Deserialize the record with a provider that notes whether any
SharedImage was opened, including by nested records. If it was, resolve
the shader for this use only: don't create a cache entry and don't use
an existing one.

Also reject shaders other than image shaders that carry an image, which
clients never serialize.

Bug: 574410140
Change-Id: Ie03077fb7a8713ecc69c3052abe539d05b2e74f2
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8727052
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1739074}
(cherry picked from commit 84831be73739894554d0a078096bb6a801ba68e6)

